# RSVD Mobile Readiness

**Remember on every change:** this product will ship to the **Apple App Store and Google Play** after web 1차 검증. Prefer structures and APIs that stay portable to a native shell.

Source of truth: [docs/ARCHITECTURE.md](docs/ARCHITECTURE.md)

## Direction

- Build and validate on **web** first (Next.js mobile shell).
- After 1차 검증, ship **iOS/Android** (prefer Capacitor/WebView shell sharing the same routes; avoid premature RN monorepo).
- When choosing between a web-only shortcut and a portable approach, choose the portable one unless the user explicitly wants a temporary hack.

## Always

- Put types, pure helpers, and product copy in `src/domain/` (no React/Next/DOM).
- Put path builders in `src/lib/routes.ts` and use them for navigation / future deep links.
- Keep `src/app/` pages thin; UI in `src/components/`; sample/API data in `src/data/`.
- Touch-first mobile shell: max width ~480px, `dvh` viewport, adequate tap targets.

## Never

- Embed business rules only in JSX (e.g. like-count minimum, reservation system copy).
- Hardcode `/space/...` strings when `routes` helpers exist.
- Add web-only APIs inside `src/domain/`.
